00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.829 align:start position:0%
since 1997 blizzard's diablo series has  been a much beloved pc staple offering  up hundreds of hours of fast-paced  dungeon crawling and loot grinding set  in a dark fantasy world overrun by  demons and other monstrous creatures now  however diablo is preparing for its most  ambitious and widespread release yet  mobile announced back in 2018 to fan  shock and even frustration do you guys  not have phone the first pocket size  diablo game is almost upon us so here is  everything you need to know about diablo  immortal for all you diablo fans who  can't get enough of the grim dark world  of sanctuary you'll be pleased to know  that diablo immortal actually fleshes  out the time period between diablo 2 and  diablo 3 a bit more than we've  previously seen  set 5 years after the events of diablo 2  a mortal takes place in the town of  wortham a sleepy little village of  hardly any consequence at all until it's  threatened by hordes of cultists and the  undead players then learn from diablo  fan favorite deckard kane that to  restore peace to the hamlet and  subsequently the world they must travel  across sanctuary to track down and  destroy shards of the world stone  preventing a necrotic calamity however  in the midst of all that chaos is yet  another struggle the conflict between  the immortals and the shadows referred  to as the cycle of strife  according to the game's lore the  conflict first began when a powerful  woman named the odessa the builder gave  birth to two children keon and akiba  to her son keon she gifted an artifact  known as the eternal crown and bestowed  upon him the responsibility of  protecting sanctuary from the undead  ultimately keon used his power and the  crown to create the immortals an  organization focused on protecting the  realm  however to her daughter akiba dedesa  gave an even greater responsibility to  live in the shadows constantly  challenging and testing her brother's  vigilance in order to ensure the  immortals were always worthy of their  station  akiba thus formed a group known as the  shadows with the understanding that if  they were ever able to overtake the  immortals they would then become  immortals themselves so with all that  going on you'll be set out into the  world and you'll get to explore areas  like ash world cemetery the dark woods  the chansar sea mount zavin and the  frozen tundra while diablo immortal  retains the action role-playing elements  in isometric perspective synonymous with  the series what sets it apart from its  predecessors is that it's a free-to-play  mobile-based mmo and is therefore  structured to accommodate that style of  gameplay  blizzard has confirmed that while the  game will have dungeons not dissimilar  to those found in the pc and console  games they will be quite a bit shorter  averaging 10 to 15 minutes in length to  make them more digestible for mobile  players the studio also confirmed that  much like world of warcraft and other  mmos you will be able to see other  characters on the map and use voice chat  to communicate with friends adding a new  level of interactivity to the series  lastly immortal has also done away with  the series mana system in favor of a  cooldown system that's more in line with  traditional mmos but promises it will  never turn to an energy system that  limits the amount of free play time a  player can sync into the game in a  single day a frequent complaint with  mobile games  the gameplay is also designed to be  played on the touchscreen so it will  feature virtual overlay controls though  it will also support keyboard and mouse  as well as a connected gamepad another  notable change too is that you can  actually move and attack simultaneously  which is not something you could do in  previous games upon starting a mortal  players can choose from 6 returning  character classes each with 12 unique  skills to unlock barbarian wizard monk  necromancer demon hunter and crusader  throughout the campaign players will  gain experience points that allow them  to increase their level up to the game's  current level cap of 60. once they hit  level 60 you can then achieve paragon  levels which can be invested into four  different skill trees survivor treasure  hunter vanquisher and gladiator  blizzard has already confirmed that it  plans on increasing the level cap adding  even more abilities and implementing  battle passes in the game as well  while the core of immortals is single  player it also boasts several  multiplayer activities as well players  will be allowed to join up in parties of  four to play through dynamic events  together in order to take on tougher  dungeons and earn better loot further at  level 45 players will unlock the  heliquery where they can hunt trap and  beat boss demons in 8 player party raids  which when completed can grant character  bonuses the development team hopes to  introduce new bosses every single month  the game also features pvp modes  including a basic 8 vs 8 battleground  mode and the cycle of strife a pvp  system open to players who have reached  immortals end game here players can join  either the immortals or shadows faction  or simply be adventurers shadows will  work to offset immortal players by  completing different shadows activities  while immortals will do the same one  example that the developers gave of  these activities was kion's ordeal a 48  player raid with groups of 12 players  fighting four bosses at the same time  once the shadows have progressed against  the immortals enough the right of exile  will trigger where the top player from  the immortals will become a boss and  must defeat the top 30 shadows players  in a 30v1 battle if the immortals win  nothing changes but if the shadows win  all 30 players are resurrected in a  battle royale to decide which shadow  clan becomes the new immortals starting  a new cycle the diablo immortal team  plans for these cycles to last between  one and three months at a time while the  diablo games might be known for their pc  presence blizzard initially stated that  diablo immortal would strictly be a  mobile game a fact that caused a lot of  tension back when it was announced  however blizzard eventually announced  that the game will be coming to pc  meaning that you'll be able to  experience diablo mortal on its home  turf there will even be cross play  meaning that you can switch where you  want to murder the forces of hell at  your will  even beyond that while there's been  little specifics there will also be  cross progression meaning that most  likely you'll be able to play as your  character on both pc and mobile letting  you jump back and forth between the two  platforms without losing any experience  or loot on top of that as the game was  initially designed for mobile the game  won't be too taxing on any pc so as long  as you have a basic setup you should be  good to go  though to note the game will be in open  beta on pc at launch sadly however no  announcement of if the game will be  coming to consoles has yet been  forthcoming  since diablo immortal was a mobile game  first it is completely free to play  meaning you don't have to pay a single  dime to kill some demons  even further blizzard stated that the  game would also not include any  pay-to-win mechanics but you know diablo  players are used to grinding their way  through levels however there will be a  battle pass with free and paid tracks  there are 40 free and 40 paid ranks each  requiring battle points to unlock which  you earn by completing specific  activities there will also be a 5 option  to unlock the battle pass while 15  unlocks 14 ranks as for the release date  diablo immortal is set to launch on june  2nd 2022 at 10am pdt in most areas of  the world on mobile it will be released  in full but on pc it will still be an  open beta blizzard did note however that  some folks may notice the game rolling  out on the apple app store and google  play starting june 1st so keep your eyes  peeled if you want to download the game  early  further diablo immortal will launch an  open beta on pc android and ios in some  asian pacific regions on june 22 pdt  including hong kong indonesia macau  malaysia the philippines singapore  taiwan and thailand immortal will also  launch on that same day in vietnam but  for pc and open beta only  and all of those regions will receive  dedicated game servers if you want to  play diablo immortal on pc you can  preload the game on your computer from  battle.net right now so as soon as the  game launches on june 2nd you can be  ready to go at the first possible moment  sadly as it's free to play you're out of  luck if you're looking for a fancy  steelbook game case or some sweet  pre-order swag however you can  pre-register to play the game at diablo  immortal's official website at this  point most of the beta tests and other  benefits have already passed from  pre-registering but there may be other  rewards and news that you may get by  doing so also before we wrap up it's  worth mentioning that activision  blizzard has been in the news a lot  lately and not just because it was  acquired by microsoft it's also  currently facing ongoing allegations of  harassment leveled against the company  in general as well as general ethics  violations as well as misconduct  allegations leveled at current ceo bobby  coddick if you want to learn more about  that situation we have linked further  information in the description that goes  into detail  and that's everything we have about the  upcoming diablo immortal it's been a  rocky road for this game pre-release but  hopefully once it's out in your hands  literally it'll still prove worthy of  the name diablo for more on diablo  immortal as well as everything in the  series make sure you subscribe to the  channel right here on gamespot until  next time thanks for watching
 

